Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.36,0:00:12.54,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(229,269)}Justina, Lady Elaine’s death is truly grievous,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.36,0:00:12.54,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(232,304)}but arresting the Tears of Blood on that alone
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.36,0:00:12.54,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(112,339)}seems excessive.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.61,0:00:21.78,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(254,269)}I am well aware. I will accept whatever punishment
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.61,0:00:21.78,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(247,304)}the Great Priestess imposes upon me. However...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.85,0:00:23.39,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(85,269)}What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.02,0:00:31.09,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(251,269)}Because I had doubts about why they went there...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.02,0:00:31.09,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(208,303)}That's why I made that absurd claim and
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.02,0:00:31.09,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(136,339)}carried out the arrests.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.09,0:00:37.40,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(244,269)}Since you, Great Priestess, and Calintz are close,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.09,0:00:37.40,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(269,305)}I thought perhaps he might open up to you right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.47,0:00:47.24,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(236,269)}I don't know the details, but the Hero of Water
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.47,0:00:47.24,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(223,304)}was an immortal being. There is no way the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.47,0:00:47.24,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(300,339)}Tears of Blood had the power to bring such a person to death.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.24,0:00:52.88,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(239,269)}It's highly likely that someone else interviewed,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.24,0:00:52.88,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(209,304)}and the Tears of Blood were just pawns.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.95,0:01:05.99,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(247,269)}In the end, Calintz didn't say a single word to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.95,0:01:05.99,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(280,304)}He said he would accept whatever judgment was passed,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.95,0:01:05.99,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(200,339}but that is no reason to hold him here.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.99,0:01:18.74,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(271,269)}Indeed, Calintz’s recent conduct is highly questionable.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.99,0:01:18.74,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(253,305)}Therefore, Justina, I must ask that you remain with
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.99,0:01:18.74,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(236,340)}the Tears of Blood and watch over him closely.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.74,0:01:29.95,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(216,269)}Lest he fall into anything dangerous.‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎ 
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.74,0:01:29.95,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(241,304)}To me, the boy is no different from my own son,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.74,0:01:29.95,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(115,339)}just as Agreian is.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.02,0:01:32.05,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(93,269)}Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.12,0:01:33.22,Nanum Barun Gothic,,0,0,0,,{\pos(106,269)}Lady Ladrinne?
